  <data key="d36">Spikes in battlefield kinetic intensity produce immediate uncertainty about conflict spillovers, sanctions and energy disruptions, triggering rapid repricing and higher implied and realized volatility across fixed‑income markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_monetary_str</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_escalation" target="global_bond_monetary_str::long_term_yield" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Acute escalation drives risk‑off flows into core long‑dated sovereign bonds (flight to quality/duration), increasing demand and pushing long‑term yields down in the short term.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_monetary_str</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_escalation" target="gulf_redsea_shipping::benchmark_oil_price_leve" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A spike in kinetic operations in the Russia–Ukraine theater (notably strikes on ports, terminals, or export infrastructure) tightens near‑term energy supply expectations and risk premia in global markets, lifting benchmark oil prices.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">gulf_redsea_shipping</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_escalation" target="us_china_tech_trade::investment_into_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in kinetic activity raise perceived strategic risk and urgency, prompting governments and defense firms to accelerate funding and procurement of AI R&amp;D, startups and defense‑oriented AI capabilities, drawing wider private and public capital into the sector.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_escalation" target="us_economic_statecraft::supply_chain_disruption" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Intense strikes on ports, rail, energy and logistics nodes in and around the theater directly interrupt export flows and transit corridors, causing immediate rerouting, congestion and shortages that raise supply‑chain disruption levels affecting U.S. supply lines and global intermediate goods.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_economic_statecraft</data>
