  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in global long-term yields increases borrowing and discounting costs for buyers and firms, depresses investment and demand for goods, and thus reduces bilateral import/export volumes over the following quarters.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_monetary_str</data>
  <data key="d39">us_economic_statecraft</data>
