<edge source="global_bond_monetary_str::repo_market_liquidity" target="gulf_redsea_shipping::maritime_chokepoint_cong" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Acute repo market illiquidity forces banks and logistics firms to pull back short‑term credit and pre‑financing for freight and bunkering, causing delayed clearances and bunching of sailings that increase congestion at chokepoints.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_monetary_str</data>
  <data key="d39">gulf_redsea_shipping</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_monetary_str::repo_market_liquidity" target="russia_ukraine_war::arms_transfer_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter repo market liquidity raises short-term funding costs for exporters and trading houses that underwrite arms shipments and inventory, while a liquidity easing lowers those frictions and directly increases the volume and velocity of transfers.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_monetary_str</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_monetary_str::repo_market_liquidity" target="us_china_tech_trade::compute_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter repo liquidity constrains short-term funding for data‑center operators, cloud providers and equipment financiers, delaying hardware purchases and capacity expansions that add compute.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_monetary_str</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_monetary_str::repo_market_liquidity" target="us_economic_statecraft::supply_chain_disruption" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A sudden drying up of repo liquidity raises short-term funding costs for banks and reduces availability of trade finance and working-capital lines for importers/exporters, causing payment delays, order cancellations and immediate interruptions in cross-border shipments.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_monetary_str</data>
  <data key="d39">us_economic_statecraft</data>
</edge>
