<edge source="global_bond_monetary_str::cross_border_flows" target="gulf_redsea_shipping::shipping_traffic_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A sudden net withdrawal of cross‑border capital reduces availability of trade finance (letters of credit and working capital) for Gulf exporters and importers, prompting shipment deferrals and a measurable drop in commercial transits through the Red Sea/Gulf routes.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_monetary_str</data>
  <data key="d39">gulf_redsea_shipping</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_monetary_str::cross_border_flows" target="russia_ukraine_war::arms_transfer_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in cross-border capital flows restores trade finance and payment channels for defense suppliers and intermediaries, directly enabling larger and faster weapons purchases and deliveries to the theater.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_monetary_str</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_monetary_str::cross_border_flows" target="us_china_tech_trade::chip_supply_constraint" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A decline in cross-border capital and trade flows reduces financing for fabs and limits inventory arbitrage across regions, increasing localized shortages and overall chip/memory tightness within a supply‑chain adjustment period.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_monetary_str</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_monetary_str::cross_border_flows" target="us_economic_statecraft::supply_chain_disruption" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Sharp capital outflows from a supplier country create FX shortages and force firms to curtail production or lose access to trade credit, producing production stoppages and missed deliveries that disrupt U.S. supply chains.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_monetary_str</data>
  <data key="d39">us_economic_statecraft</data>
</edge>
