<edge source="us_economic_statecraft::non_tariff_intensity" target="global_bond_monetary_str::repo_market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Expanded non-tariff measures (e.g., financial sanctions, bans, tighter cross-border compliance) shrink the pool of eligible collateral and correspondent-banking links, raising haircuts and prompting banks to hoard liquidity, which reduces repo-market depth.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_economic_statecraft</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_monetary_str</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_economic_statecraft::non_tariff_intensity" target="russia_ukraine_war::arms_transfer_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Expanded export controls, licensing bans, and regulatory barriers increase legal and logistical costs for intermediaries and foreign suppliers, directly reducing the volume of weapons, dual‑use components, and related transfers into Russia or its proxies.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_economic_statecraft</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_economic_statecraft::non_tariff_intensity" target="us_china_tech_trade::chip_supply_constraint" id="0">
